 "q-42535" :question/id #uuid "defa3304-fe74-57d6-89db-cdb756b4b384" :question/math-academy-id "q-42535" :question/problem "Consider $E=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]$ and a $3\\times 3$ matrix $A.$ Find the row operation that, when applied to $A,$ is equivalent to multiplying $A$ by the given elementary matrix $E$ from the left." :question/worked-solution "The given matrix $E$ is obtained by swapping the first and the third rows of ${I}_{3}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =E\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $EA$ is equivalent to applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{1}↔{R}_{3}$ to $A.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-42535/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b0341b26-9c91-5b8a-a917-20129155e336"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-42535"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-110458/selection/ce7b91be1786af9146a93f6c1c884f92aa2bcd55cc17fd3d64073cd70366ec36" :answer/id #uuid "c8e1653d-049a-5a99-a575-79bb50ac6684" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{R}_{1}:=5{R}_{1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110458/selection/e321f10ce60d7f4adf0e7aa0e3cbffa994f0b6664e66dc791e9b2e0c01dffafb" :answer/id #uuid "5f24933a-8220-5161-8c61-c8f9db24486c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{R}_{1}:=\\frac{1}{5}{R}_{1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110458/selection/e44de9d87f5cb4e031a2f90522975ce1bf732ca9d0090d0be2b7781937eaf274" :answer/id #uuid "601ef09b-7902-5474-ba11-b036602e1d77" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+5{R}_{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110458/selection/63213d6cf165ec26f6c78d3bf1aa6eb843c3bafbbdfc3b2387d41497512dffd1" :answer/id #uuid "73f353ff-9c21-5414-8d6e-0592b6