r/id #uuid "0f916f63-4965-5fcd-b5f4-8141b3f101fb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110487/selection/5b0d8251e3234296af015a4f96e19179da7bceaadc9aed4c59278bb4ac344a69" :answer/id #uuid "4f384f54-45df-58d0-96a8-d779b4befff9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -4\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110487/selection/2b517e5a95d3c803dce945860e6150c72eefd7ad1e8403ca064388936d234eff" :answer/id #uuid "d6345991-0351-5ceb-9f16-70ae9dab716c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -4\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110487/selection/1fd7b82cf1259fe640e372e609321da8c7303a92ab91864e54bc1fdd9a75d9ad" :answer/id #uuid "fd45dd00-0398-5ff7-8cbf-0f733d30eac4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110487/selection/e2a9286272e476005b439c14842df37f1d926637607a963005488ce712e87ea1" :answer/id #uuid "11dd4d5e-f196-51a8-b6bb-366dbcd7bd9e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -4\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110487/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "79976de3-9144-5a78-9435-02580daabca4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-110487/selection/5b0d8251e3234296af015a4f96e19179da7bceaadc9aed4c59278bb4ac344a69" :answer-field/choices ["q-110487/selection/fd5c6bf0fded7bfebb31242a7121b15eddfc74bc85e9080fa76e60df49b42c62" "q-110487/selection/5b0d8251e3234296af015a4f96e19179da7bceaadc9aed4c59278bb4ac344a69" "q-110487/selection/2b517e5a95d3c803dce945860e6150c72eefd7ad1e8403ca064388936d234eff" "q-110487/selection/1fd7b82cf1259fe640e372e609321da8c7303a92ab91864e54bc1fdd9a75d9ad" "q-110487/selection/e2a9286272e476005b439c14842df37f1d926637607a963005488ce712e87ea1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-110487" :question/id #uuid "81e02727-aa2a-5c53-aca2-5643c7656f5b" :question/math-academy-id "q-110487" :question/problem "Suppose that the following elementary row operations are applied to a $3\\times 3$ matrix $A$ in the given order:\n\n$$\n{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1},\\,{R}_{3}:=-4{R}_{3}\n$$\n\nWhat is the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication?" :question/worked-solution "First, let's find the elementary matrices corresponding to the given elementary row operations.\n\n- The first operation is ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1}.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={E}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The second operation is ${R}_{3}:=-4{R}_{3}.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :=-4{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={E}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo apply the first elementary row operation to the matrix $A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{1}$ on the left and get ${E}_{1}A:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$\n\nThen, to apply the second elementary row operation to ${E}_{1}A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{2}$ on the left and get ${E}_{2}{E}_{1}A:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -4\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-110487/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "00b69189-1ae1-5625-adfb-e5460845c776"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-110487"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-110492/selection/ec1bb805db55c2378919c8c2ca62fb596dae1354dbbdbca7bfc344e630d06e34" :answer/id #uuid "01617865-e9f1-5eb7-9d86-5d4abf648668" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 9\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110492/selection/73172cd7276dba1d8d3ce1140e46b7f876f3815e8aba2200ab785ff266e01ff0" :answer/id #uuid "aaac07f3-084b-591b-ad2d-edc58aab5032" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 9\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110492/selection/2b6bb62255241cd638a63d221b5d2649943f885c3475efd272dabf7430883931" :answer/id #uuid "b3a87281-ecea-537c-a221-931d5357f342" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 