following elementary row operations are applied to a $3\\times 3$ matrix $A$ in the given order:\n\n$$\n{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+(-2){R}_{2},\\,{R}_{2}↔{R}_{3},\\,{R}_{3}:=9{R}_{3}\n$$\n\nWhat is the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication?" :question/worked-solution "First, let's find the elementary matrices corresponding to the given elementary row operations.\n\n- The first operation is ${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+(-2){R}_{2}.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-2){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={E}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The second operation is ${R}_{2}↔{R}_{3}.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={E}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The third operation is ${R}_{3}:=9{R}_{3}.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :=9{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 9\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={E}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo apply the first elementary row operation to the matrix $A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{1}$ on the left and get ${E}_{1}A:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$\n\nThen, to apply the second elementary row operation to ${E}_{1}A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{2}$ on the left and get ${E}_{2}{E}_{1}A:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$\n\nFinally, to apply the third elementary row operation to ${E}_{2}{E}_{1}A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{3}$ on the left and get ${E}_{3}{E}_{2}{E}_{1}A:$ \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 9\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-110492/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "00b69189-1ae1-5625-adfb-e5460845c776"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-110492"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-32148/selection/ee86edb0abd64179a967a42ad25792632b57f91533289790c1f19036e928866f" :answer/id #uuid "869bc468-3bcb-5ca2-9e7b-588b624f601d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-32148/selection/f9f2ed88c5273141a43efffcbcacf50a7133e4451648ab734a6d8b5818e5ec96" :answer/id #uuid "0016ba65-d689-5946-8896-7492ea0d4cdf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-32148/selection/59eb35db85f6749719a0b7cbbd75d22bc66c17973e57d3ac6cad700c0d838da6" :answer/id #uuid "ad0416ce-f9b7-54b0-af07-5d034a3ac5de" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -4\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-32148/selection/5e19a90ad5f79aa21b23b4e6596035914f393cce7c4aa85d444c9f4f5e8d1b78" :answer/id #uuid "a20a3460-da0e-56b5-b9d3-b319c0aff0c6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -5\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -5\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-32148/selection/07116dc3508bb01e3085441cfbce93afc620efc06c36f9a2117d166bd14895dd" :answer/id #uuid "fbc905c4-81f8-55c0-a82b-e1d829bdba10" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-32148/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "c057c6fc-dc12-5ba1-96ab-d43e72eef16d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-32148/selection/ee86edb0abd64179a967a42ad25792632b57f91533289790c1f19036e928866f" :answer-field/choices ["q-32148/selection/ee86edb0abd64179a967a42ad25792632b57f91533289790c1f19036e928866f" "q-32148/selection/f9f2ed88c5273141a43efffcbcacf50a7133e4451648ab734a6d8b5818e5ec96" "q-32148/selection/59eb35db85f6749719a0b7cbbd75d22bc66c17973e57d3ac6cad700c0d838da6" "q-32148/selection/5e19a90ad5f79aa21b23b4e6596035914f393cce7c4aa85d444c9f4f5e8d1b78" "q-32148/selection/07116dc3508bb01e3085441cfbce93afc620efc06c36f9a2117d166bd14895dd"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-32148" :question/id #uuid "ec5f1c66-f277-50e6-aa88-1dab289d722b" :question/math-academy-id "q-32148" :question/problem "Suppose that the following elementary row operations are applied to a $3\\times 3$ matrix $A$ in the given order:\n\n$$\n{R}_{1}:=-5{R}_{1},\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-4{R}_{3}\n$$\n\nWhat is the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication?" :question/worked-solution "First, let's find the elementary matrices corresponding to the given elementary row operations.\n\n- The first operation is ${R}_{1}:=-5{R}_{1}.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=-5{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={E}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The second operation is ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-4{R}_{3}.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-4{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={E}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo apply the first elementary row operation to the matrix $A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{1}$ on the left and get ${E}_{1}A:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$\n\nThen, to apply the second elementary row operation to ${E}_{1}A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{2}$ on the left and get ${E}_{2}{E}_{1}A:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-32148/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "00b69189-1ae1-5625-adfb-e5460845c776"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-32148"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-110494/selection/7d45a36f42196adf5229f4bf3fc104093d54f8bbaf45d18758ad32b2cb9ec27b" :answer/id #uuid "545706cb-5f61-5378-bdab-7c17c92cd12d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 8 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110494/selection/ad94fd5e4879148298824acd9c29f6edfd76cb7e6fb0c736d093bf943ab73207" :answer/id #uuid "e38dbbf3-8051-5b6a-865a-b165bd011f0e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 8 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -\\frac{1}{2} & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110494/selection/0c164eabfdf52004dc0d04ddd36c441f2c436ca94459d2bb04de55827d990f3a" :answer/id #uuid "5adb49ef-8bb5-5ffa-90d7-6ffd7b42de3c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 8 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110494/selection/91cf68d5dac5d19941fbb5d57406026fa9dfb008f9ffbe022af3d43d1946e858" :answer/id #uuid "f64f3902-73f9-5252-a5e3-fb379ee12f00" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 8 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -\\frac{1}{2} & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110494/selection/66f510f4835cc31d2e0359dfc92d1b2bec41281d9ff36f2282ebee5605c9fcc8" :answer/id #uuid "974c22c3-0356-5655-bd1e-9feee3d6d619" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 8 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110494/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "97d58cc1-1b46-565e-844b-deff17ded11b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-110494/selection/7d45a36f42196adf5229f4bf3fc104093d54f8bbaf45d18758ad32b2cb9ec27b" :answer-field/choices ["q-110494/selection/7d45a36f42196adf5229f4bf3fc104093d54f8bbaf45d18758ad32b2cb9ec27b" "q-110494/selection/ad94fd5e4879148298824acd9c29f6edfd76cb7e6fb0c736d093bf943ab73207" "q-110494/selection/0c164eabfdf52004dc0d04ddd36c441f2c436ca94459d2bb04de55827d990f3a" "q-110494/selection/91cf68d5dac5d19941fbb5d57406026fa9dfb008f9ffbe022af3d43d1946e858" "q-110494/selection/66f510f4835cc31d2e0359dfc92d1b2bec41281d9ff36f2282ebee5605c9fcc8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-110494" :question/id #uuid "d31e1efe-db86-5d29-87ec-eb9ae72af647" :question/math-academy-id "q-110494" :question/problem "Suppose that the following elementary row operations are applied to a $3\\times 3$ matrix $A$ in the given order:\n\n$$\n{R}_{1}↔{R}_{2},\\,{R}_{3}:=-\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{3},\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+8{R}_{1}\n$$\n\nWhat is the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication?" :question/worked-solution "First, let's find the elementary matrices corresponding to the given elementary row operations.\n\n- The first operation is ${R}_{1}↔{R}_{2}.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={E}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The second operation is ${R}_{3}:=-\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{3}.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :=-\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={E}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The third operation is ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+8{R}_{1}.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+8{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 8 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={E}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo apply the first elementary row operation to the matrix $A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{1}$ on the left and get ${E}_{1}A:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$\n\nThen, to apply the second elementary row operation to ${E}_{1}A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{2}$ on the left and get ${E}_{2}{E}_{1}A:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$\n\nFinally, to apply the third elementary row operation to ${E}_{2}{E}_{1}A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{3}$ on the left and get ${E}_{3}{E}_{2}{E}_{1}A:$ \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 8 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-110494/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "00b69189-1ae1-5625-adfb-e5460845c776"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-110494"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-42512/selection/0287a5fc697cc357557bc43c65cc4facf2a4e47b8c71410ce64baccd43069fe8" :answer/id #uuid "1d288367-87ac-5577-bbfa-c3d34f5e2527" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-42512/selection/93304c02252b34aa57779af51948b85a15428af21208e6a2bc1eca5a9001be1e" :answer/id #uuid "f4e4cdfe-b953-573f-b13a-9dda3d4c621d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-42512/selection/5874384b770eb1671394844de856f69091c9351b0c13635443d8af08bee83977" :answer/id #uuid "f2231513-d371-5a41-8753-48ce2d6ffeef" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-42512/selection/c2cbe1869776e597b4799c39d401b71c3aa7c8d3c5fefc2070c41c3adee0ade9" :answer/id #uuid "74113b01-bf7e-545c-beea-560f8be80865" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-42512/selection/e671ee1f4824c48b2a846fbb729657b654b419d9d1907f97f37fbb3b21cd2c05" :answer/id #uuid "2752f5fc-0fc9-544d-98e2-7ac8f281221e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-42512/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "d069d958-32e1-5738-8d57-ceb01abe88a6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-42512/selection/c2cbe1869776e597b4799c39d401b71c3aa7c8d3c5fefc2070c41c3adee0ade9" :answer-field/choices ["q-42512/selection/0287a5fc697cc357557bc43c65cc4facf2a4e47b8c71410ce64baccd43069fe8" "q-42512/selection/93304c02252b34aa57779af51948b85a15428af21208e6a2bc1eca5a9001be1e" "q-42512/selection/5874384b770eb1671394844de856f69091c9351b0c13635443d8af08bee83977" "q-42512/selection/c2cbe1869776e597b4799c39d401b71c3aa7c8d3c5fefc2070c41c3adee0ade9" "q-42512/selection/e671ee1f4824c48b2a846fbb729657b654b419d9d1907f97f37fbb3b21cd2c05"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-42512" :question/id #uuid "64e9bfae-8824-55ac-8d3c-9ad9a8753027" :question/math-academy-id "q-42512" :question/problem "Suppose that the following elementary row operations are applied to a $3\\times 3$ matrix $A$ in the given order:\n\n$$\n{R}_{2}↔{R}_{3},\\,{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+2{R}_{1},\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-2{R}_{1}\n$$\n\nWhat is the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication?" :question/worked-solution "First, let's find the elementary matrices corresponding to the given elementary row operations.\n\n- The first operation is ${R}_{2}↔{R}_{3}.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={E}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The second operation is ${R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+2{R}_{1}.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={E}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The third operation is ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-2{R}_{1}.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={E}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo apply the first elementary row operation to the matrix $A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{1}$ on the left and get ${E}_{1}A:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$\n\nThen, to apply the second elementary row operation to ${E}_{1}A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{2}$ on the left and get ${E}_{2}{E}_{1}A:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$\n\nFinally, to apply the third elementary row operation to ${E}_{2}{E}_{1}A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{3}$ on the left and get ${E}_{3}{E}_{2}{E}_{1}A:$ \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-42512/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "00b69189-1ae1-5625-adfb-e5460845c776"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-42512"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-4732"] :question/problem "Consider ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060012/assets/ba3f1852b12b6f4a246a855c88c9b867b7e750c6dddf350cab0324629fc047c4.png) and a $3\\times 3$ matrix $A.$\nFind the row operation that, when applied to $A,$ is equivalent to multiplying $A$ by the given elementary matrix $E$ from the left." :question/worked-solution "The given matrix $E$ is obtained by taking the second row of $I$ and adding $7$ times the third row:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+7{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =E\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $EA$ is equivalent to applying the elementary \nrow operation $R_2 :=R_2+7R_3$ to $A.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-4733"] :question/problem "Suppose we are applying the elementary row operation $R_2:=R_2-2R_1$ to a $3\\times 3$ matrix $A.$ What is the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication?" :question/worked-solution "We need to find a matrix $E$ such that $EA$ is equivalent to applying the elementary row operation $R_2 := R_2-2R_1$ to $A.$\n\nTo find $E,$ we apply the given row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =E\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication is $EA\\mathbin{:}$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060012/assets/8d015aca8950073c165d53b14f86f0e65a207438ad901ce82f85f65bb8347519.png)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-4734"] :question/problem "Suppose we are applying these two elementary row operations, in the given order, to a $3\\times 3$ matrix $A\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\nR_2\\leftrightarrow R_3, \\qquad\n\tR_1:=6R_1\n$$\n\nFind the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication." :question/worked-solution "First, let's find the elementary matrices corresponding to the two given elementary row operations.\n\n- The first operation is $R_2\\leftrightarrow R_3.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={E}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The second operation is $R_1:=6R_1.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=6{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}6 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={E}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo apply the first elementary row operation to the matrix $A,$ we multiply by $E_1$ on the left and get $E_1 A\\mathbin{:}$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060012/assets/375f1950c460b1f310fa279f6d7f203f88ff641000715dfaec192f47d785aa93.png)\n\nThen, to apply the second elementary row operation to $E_1 A,$ we multiply by $E_2$ on the left and get $E_2 E_1 A\\mathbin{:}$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060012/assets/6357cc2a2526f38a0f0f7e2e7ef4ee7a1a564adfa70264028ff732f44ba7b763.png)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
